{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795629792,"nonce":"5IgMNLI2QPo5uluFjofTnnDr8wQ=","title":"Code editor: nothing should look scrollable when the text fits","message":"Reported by use: \"scrollbar should be hidden by default in code editor when the height fits the content\".\n\nMeasured headless: where the content fits, no scrollbar is drawn (3 lines in 200 px, auto height, a folded block that makes 15 lines fit 320 px). The minimap did draw its view box over the whole of a text that fits; that box is now hidden then.\n\nOne case still shows a bar: the cn_demo editor, 15 lines at 19.5 px plus 16 px padding top and bottom is 324.5 px in a 320 px box. Every line is visible and only padding is cut, yet the view scrolls by 4.5 px and the bar shows during the scroll. If that is what was seen, one option is to treat an overflow no larger than the bottom padding as fitting. Waiting to confirm what was seen.","files":null}]}